 ],
 "literal": "Spirit-possession dance as realized Velan, remedy / not knowing becoming, mother to see, / intense distress and grief today we suffer even if, / may he not come indeed, O friend, to the slope / female elephant's trunk like large ears of millet / eating parrots chasing mountain woman's hand rattle / on the mountain side resounding grove / shining mountain lord, in the night.",
 "translation": "O friend, let the lord of the shining mountains not come in the night! Even if we must suffer today from this intense distress and grief, while mother watches the priest Velan—who thinks my illness is due to spirit-possession—fail to find a cure. Let him not journey through the slopes where the rattles in the hands of mountain women, used to scare away parrots eating the millet with ears as large as female elephants' trunks, resound through the groves on the mountain side.",
 "modern": "தோழியே! என் நோய் வெறியாட்டு என்று நினைத்து வேலன் அதற்குரிய மருந்தினை அறியாமல் தவிப்பதை அன்னை பார்ப்பதால், நாம் இன்று மிகுந்த துன்பத்தை அனுபவித்தாலும் பரவாயில்லை; விளங்கும் மலைநாட்டை உடைய தலைவன் இரவில் இங்கு வர வேண்டாம். பெண் யானையின் துதிக்கை போன்ற பெரிய கதிர்களைக் கொண்ட தினையை உண்ண வரும் கிளிகளை விரட்டும் குறிஞ்சி நிலப் பெண்ணின் கையில் உள்ள குளிரென்னும் கருவியின் ஒலி, மலைப்பக்கத்துச் சோலையெங்கும் எதிரொலிக்கும் அத்தகைய மலைநாடன் இரவில் வர வேண்டாம்.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her close friend in the Kurinji (mountainous) landscape. Her mother, noticing her physical decline, assumes she is possessed by a spirit and summons the priest Velan to perform a ritual dance. The priest, however, does not know the true cause of her illness, which is her secret love and separation from the hero. Although the heroine suffers from this misunderstanding and the impending ritual, she is more concerned about the hero's safety. She begs her friend that the lord of the shining mountains should not make the dangerous journey to meet her at night. The image of the mountain woman's rattle echoing through the groves highlights the dangers and alertness of the mountain slopes, warning that his secret visits are highly risky.",
